      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rockville_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After the 1814 Treaty of Fort Jackson, settlers moved into the area that became Rockville, part of Clarke County’s early expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        8,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rockville_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Clarke County’s steamboat era, beginning with the 1818 launch of the Alabama steamboat, influenced Rockville’s early river trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rockville_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Rockville’s lowland soils near the Alabama River historically supported cotton and livestock, thanks to the fertile floodplain.",
